<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7126" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνά-παιστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		(cf. sq.) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hammered, forged,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					2.678<i>B</i>64
				</span></i>
			, al., <i><span class="en">
				11.161<i>A</i>94
			</span></i> (Delos, <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>struck back, rebounding:</i>—as Subst.,
				<i>anapaest</i> (i. e. a dactyl <i>reversed</i>), <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Heph.
				8
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀπὸ μείζους</span>”
				<i>dactyl,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristid.Quint.
					1.15
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>anapaestic verse,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1452b23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				1.25
			</span></i>, etc.: in pl., of the Comic <i>parabasis,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				504
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pax</u>
				735
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάπαιστοι σύμπτυκτοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pherecr.
					79
				</span></i>
			, cf. Sch.metr.<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				4.1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάπαιστόν τι</span> something
				<i>in anapaestic metre,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.158
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάπαιστα, τά,</span>
			<i>anapaestic verses,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				3.43
			</span></i>; esp. of <i>ribald</i> or <i>satirical songs,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				66.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Per.</u>
				33
			</span></i>.</div>
